// flashcard drill — JAH Baker Trade Database — What bakers do (jahdb demo program)
var ITEMS=[["What bakers do","Bakers produce breads, pastries, and desserts: mixing, fermenting, shaping, and baking at scale. Bread baking is biology \u2014 managing wild yeast and gluten. Pastry is precision \u2014 butter, temperature, and timing. Early hour"], ["Essential tools","Stand mixer, bench scraper, digital scale (non-negotiable), thermometers, proofing baskets (bannetons), baking steel or stone, lame for scoring, pastry brush, rolling pin, and sheet pans. Pros add: deck oven, sheeter, an"], ["Key skills","Baker's percentages: scaling by flour weight. Gluten development: kneading and folding. Fermentation reading: knowing when dough is ready. Shaping: tension without tearing. Scoring and steaming for crust. Lamination for "], ["Safety essentials","Burns: ovens, steam, hot pans \u2014 dry mitts always. Flour dust is explosive in quantity; control it. Heavy lifting: 50-lb flour bags need technique. Slippery floors from flour and water."], ["Getting started","Bake at home seriously first \u2014 sourdough teaches fermentation. Work in a bakery as an assistant. Culinary programs offer baking tracks. Master one category (bread, then pastry) before branching."], ["Pro tips","Weigh everything \u2014 cups lie. Temperature is an ingredient: dough temp, water temp, room temp. Keep a bake log. Fresh yeast matters. For sourdough: a strong starter beats any recipe tweak."], ["Baker's percentage","Trade term \u2014 Baker's percentage: All ingredients expressed as percent of flour weight."], ["Autolyse","Trade term \u2014 Autolyse: Resting flour and water before kneading."], ["Bulk ferment","Trade term \u2014 Bulk ferment: The first rise of the whole dough mass."], ["Stretch and fold","Trade term \u2014 Stretch and fold: Gentle gluten-building technique."], ["Shaping","Trade term \u2014 Shaping: Forming loaves with surface tension."], ["Proofing","Trade term \u2014 Proofing: The final rise before baking."], ["Scoring","Trade term \u2014 Scoring: Slashing loaves for controlled expansion."], ["Steam","Trade term \u2014 Steam: Oven steam for thin crackling crust."], ["Crumb","Trade term \u2014 Crumb: The interior structure of bread."], ["Sourdough starter","Trade term \u2014 Sourdough starter: Wild yeast and bacteria culture."], ["Levain","Trade term \u2014 Levain: The preferment built from starter."], ["Poolish","Trade term \u2014 Poolish: Wet French preferment."], ["Biga","Trade term \u2014 Biga: Stiff Italian preferment."], ["Lamination","Trade term \u2014 Lamination: Folding butter into dough for flaky layers."], ["Detrempe","Trade term \u2014 Detrempe: The dough base in lamination."], ["Beurrage","Trade term \u2014 Beurrage: The butter block in lamination."], ["Blind bake","Trade term \u2014 Blind bake: Pre-baking a crust before filling."], ["Docking","Trade term \u2014 Docking: Pricking dough to prevent bubbling."], ["Retard","Trade term \u2014 Retard: Slowing fermentation with cold."]];
